{"title":"Career Roadmap · Editor","role":"Editor","summary":"An Editor reviews, structures, improves, and prepares written or digital content for publication. With a BA in Digital Humanities / Cultural Studies, the strongest pathway combines editing + humanities research + digital publishing + cultural knowledge + communication + technology.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 UG · 2026","Current degree":"BA (General / Honours) — Digital Humanities / Cultural Studies"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Editorial intern, content/editorial assistant, copy editor, publishing assistant"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Junior Editor, Copy Editor, Digital Editor, Academic Editor or Content Editor"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Editor, Managing Editor, Commissioning Editor or Editorial Lead"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Editorial Director, Publishing Lead, Content Strategy Lead, Digital Humanities Editor or independent editorial specialist"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The role can span publishing, academic content, digital media, cultural institutions, research organisations, museums, archives, websites, journals, educational platforms, and content companies."}]},{"heading":"Career-route check","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Strong alignment, but editing is primarily a portfolio- and experience-driven profession. A BA alone does not guarantee an Editor title immediately after graduation."},{"type":"p","text":"A realistic progression is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Editorial Intern","Editorial Assistant","Junior Editor/Assistant Editor","Editor","Senior Editor","Managing/Commissioning/Content Editor"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best employability combination:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Humanities","Editing","Research","Digital Publi